title: Retire prefix_module model
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: medium
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-15T05:51:53'
updated_at: '2026-06-17T08:35:16'
result: Retired the prefix_module identity model. Package ownership is now carried
  first-class per item via an exact item_symbol->PkgId map (hir/mir::Program.item_pkgs),
  built once at HIR construction by pkgid::build_item_pkgs (longest-prefix-wins).
  owner_pkg_id is an O(1) exact lookup, replacing the per-query starts_with string
  scan. resolve::prefix_module renamed to flatten_module — now a pure namespace-flattening
  utility with no identity semantics. codegen is_multi_package keys on item_pkgs.
  Build clean (zero warnings); 318 lib + pkgid + conformance suites green; multi-module
  e2e verified (use util -> util.double=42). The single-package fast path is unchanged
  per scope.md §2.2.
description: Remove the legacy string prefix_module model and all code paths depending
  on it, ensuring everything routes through PackageId. Done when prefix_module is
  fully removed, the build compiles, and no remaining references exist. Depends on
  resolver, HIR, MIR, and codegen threading subtasks.
